DECISIONS (mine, record for review):
D-a cancel before submit ends `cancelled` at once for waiting_for_gui, create_requested, session_created, toolsets_checked, send_waiting (state_detail {reason: cancelled_before_submit, after: <state>}). Safe: the Desktop's next step is refused (bad_transition) and the window lets go quietly. Residue: a session.create already in flight may leave an empty child session.
D-b no cancel_sent column: "sent" lives in the holding window's memory; prompt.cancel is idempotent (terminal → unchanged, unknown → unknown_execution), so a new holder asks again at most once.
D-c send is allowed on `finished` and on `cancelled` runs that have a session_id (store.SENDABLE_STATES).
D-d start_send expires the old claim (claim_expires_at=now) so a window takes the follow-up at once; the generation keeps rising.
D-e runs.task/prompt_text/submission_id hold the CURRENT turn; earlier turns are archived in table `turns`; the tool view shows `turn`.
D-j reconciling submit_requested: lazy session + stored stop → `cancelled` (reason never_admitted, nothing reached Hermes); a failed toolset check in a non-lazy session → unknown/submit_unconfirmed, never refused (our turn may have run). Lazy + failed check → refused (nothing was admitted).
D-k a send_waiting run of another connection is skipped (left to it); a principal mismatch → refused identity_changed (nothing sent).
D-o dispose() gives every claim back (REST release) and never stops a run. Whether the real Desktop window unload runs ctx.onDispose to completion is NOT verified [rd only]; if it does not, takeover waits out the 180 s lease.
D-p transient = code 5001, reason runtime_draining, or no reply: not counted toward the three receipt refusals; prompt.cancel is asked again on the next track. unknown_execution and other refusals are not asked again (the receipt decides).
D-q a blocked approval's reason is read from the tool row's error text: denied | timeout | blocked (texts tools/approval.py:742-790 [rd]).
D-r default wait_seconds: cancel 30, send 60.
D-s (bug found + fixed) the pre-claim connection check now compares only the connection: in the committed code a running child stored under a non-null principal subject was skipped by every window before the claim (subject compared against none). Local routes have subject null, so it never showed. Regression unit test added.
D-t the retain (host.retainProfile) is taken in take() right after the claim and held until the run is final, the claim is lost, or the window is disposed (P5 + audit 9d). Rewritten unit claim: the k3 trace asserted a release right after the submit.
D-u P1 rewritten unit claim: k3 "fix 8" asserted lazy:false + nothing pending → unknown; that cell now repeats the identical submit after the relaxed check (orchestrator P1). The lazy:false case whose set grew stays unknown.

